        <mxCell id="c54" parent="1" style="shape=note;size=18;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=12;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;" value="&lt;b&gt;Missing details we found&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Our workflow did not say how Marco finds a returning customer. He retypes the name and licence each time.&lt;br&gt;• The workflow did not show where Marco sees whether a car is ready. We needed an overview screen behind &amp;quot;Back to overview&amp;quot;.&lt;br&gt;• It was unclear what happens if Marco picks the wrong car after submitting." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="600" x="20" y="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c55" parent="1" style="shape=note;size=18;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=12;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" value="&lt;b&gt;Group decisions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• One customer and one car per rental in the first version.&lt;br&gt;• The overview is a filtered list of today&#39;s rentals with their status. We add it as its own view.&lt;br&gt;• No editing after submitting in version 1. Changing or cancelling a rental comes later.&lt;br&gt;• Only cars that are free for the chosen dates appear in the list, so Marco cannot pick a booked car." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="176" width="600" x="660" y="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
